class:: Periodicity
summary:: Repeating-structure evidence without a final F0 decision
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Pitch2

description::
Reports the strongest normalized repeating-structure evidence in the requested lag range. code::\nsdf:: uses the strongest McLeod normalized square difference peak; code::\yin:: uses one minus the selected CMNDF minimum. The output is an algorithmic periodicity measure, not pitch confidence or probability: missing-fundamental and polyphonic signals can be strongly periodic while their F0 identity remains uncertain.

Frame scheduling, effective minimum frequency, latency, and silence behavior match the MIR2 pitch family. Silence returns zero. The closest vanilla comparison is the optional clarity-like evidence in link::Classes/Pitch::, but code::Periodicity:: is deliberately usable without accepting or retaining a frequency result.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio-rate signal.

argument:: minFreq
Minimum periodic frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Maximum periodic frequency in Hz.

argument:: frameSize
Literal power-of-two frame size from 256 through 8192.

argument:: hop
Update hop as a frame fraction from 0.0625 through 1.

argument:: method
Literal code::\nsdf:: or code::\yin::.

returns::
Periodicity from 0 through 1.

method:: latency
Returns approximate first-result latency in seconds.

instancemethods::

examples::
Periodicity reports repeating-structure evidence without requiring a commitment to an F0 decision. In this example, periodicity controls the feedback damping of a Karplus-Strong physical waveguide: periodic sustained sections produce long ringing tones, while non-periodic friction decays instantly into muted plucks. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the live periodicity index.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("texture.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var periodicity = Periodicity.kr(source, 60, 2000, 2048, 0.25, \nsdf);
        var feedback = periodicity.linlin(0.0, 1.0, 0.1, 0.98).lag(0.05);
        var waveguide = CombC.ar(source, 0.05, 110.reciprocal, feedback * 2.0);
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + (waveguide * 0.3);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, periodicity) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Periodicity", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0);
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

